   "notes": "Fischer et al. report a thermal EOS for iron-saturated FeO, not a standalone 300 K BM3. The Fe0.94O starting powder was mixed with Fe and the authors treat the equilibrated high-P-T oxide as approximately stoichiometric FeO. Reported sample temperatures already include the source's 3% downward axial-gradient correction and must be evaluated at their tabulated values. All four row-level sources for the global B1 fit are now bundled: Fischer Table S1, Seagle supplementary Table 1, Ozawa printed Table 2, and Campbell supplementary Table S2. Seagle contains 65 hcp-Fe rows, 14 fcc-Fe rows, and two rows without Fe volume that retain the source's 50 +/- 4 GPa isobar assignment; Campbell contains 10 hcp-Fe and 15 fcc-Fe rows. The exact regression weights/objective and Fischer's final combined row selection are not published. The marginal pressure range includes those comparison/fit-input studies and is not a phase-stability boundary.",
   "identifier": "feo_fischer_2011_bm3_2",
   "pressure_calibration": {
    "status": "partially_resolved",
    "methods": [
     {
      "kind": "equation_of_state",
