    "recalculation": {
     "status": "reference_eos_not_bundled",
     "notes": "Paired NaCl phase, molar volume, effective temperature and their errors are bundled for every current-study row. The exact Decker B1/Fei B2 pair is not registered as a complete executable catalog calibration route. Use the tabulated pressure; do not substitute a newer NaCl scale. Seagle fit-input rows have Fe volumes and temperatures but no NaCl readings or individual pressures."
    },
    "notes": "MAP detector angle calibrated with NaCl a=5.6402 A (JCPDS 05-0628); DAC geometry with CeO2. MAP cooling cycles minimize deviatoric stress. The article writes DAC T_sample=295+0.97*(T_meas-295) and T_NaCl=(3*T_meas+295)/4. The workbook uses a 293 K baseline for some Ni-NiO DAC runs and 295 K for others; preserve its stored values. Equation (4) prints sigma_TNaCl=(T_meas-295)/2, while the hot DAC workbook rows use (T_meas-T_ambient)/4; preserve the workbook uncertainties. The workbook pressure-threshold footnote is approximate: honor the explicit NaCl phase column, including B2 rows below 26 GPa."
   },
   "parameter_provenance": {
    "equation": "Section 4.1 Equation (5), page 560, and its immediately following gamma(V) and theta(V) definitions. BM3 reference; FeO has K0_prime fixed to 4 (BM2-equivalent reference).",
