   "notes": "All values printed in Table 1 are transcribed. Parenthesized lattice and volume values are represented as standard deviations. The paper gives one shared pressure-precision range of 0.05-0.1 GPa rather than row-wise errors; the two bounds are preserved and no single source uncertainty is invented. Temperature is the source's nominal 300 K experimental condition. Cubic volumes and their standard deviations are derived as V=a^3 and sigma_V=3a^2 sigma_a; rhombohedral equivalent-hexagonal volumes are source values. Blank cells mean that Table 1 reports no observation for that phase at that pressure.",
